] [17592186402767 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402767 1084 #uuid "a7eb10d8-4da4-5dab-bc8c-4a003f7cebfb" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402768 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402768 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402768 1084 #uuid "c70e171e-d942-5f58-90b7-b6fb6a232836" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402769 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402770 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402769 1069 "q-42020" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402769 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402769 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+y=3 \\\\  & -2x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\nII. The system has a unique solution\nIII. The system is inconsistent" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402769 1072 #uuid "1a930b2a-2578-5145-8e40-06b6cab16ba9" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402769 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds t