4 #uuid "9a831cb5-7996-50f5-a00f-9238c740dfbc" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402883 1081 "$S$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402883 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402883 1084 #uuid "965453b1-8564-5aa8-8e90-1d29787fd17c" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402884 1081 "$Q$ and $S$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402884 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402884 1084 #uuid "d8c136ae-153c-59f1-8f96-afd3d63f12c8" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402885 1081 "$Q$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402885 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402885 1084 #uuid "07ca52bf-aff6-51dc-b9d9-86e513484473" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402886 1081 "$P$ and $S$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402886 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402886 1084 #uuid "4d68e0d7-29e8-5b6d-a9f0-b295aa3c7e0e" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402887 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402888 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402887 1069 "q-47516" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402887 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402887 1071 "![](images/4e/4e796ff4d915d8c8b829574ade4eab05c7740de1f376d00900ec0d14b08f97d9.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nII. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\nIII. There are removable discontinuities at both $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402887 1072 #uuid "3f6ba6a9-669c-53ec-9eb7-450cfe9629e8" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402887 1074 "The function is continuous at $x=-1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nOn the other hand, the function has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(1)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)\\ne f(1)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=1$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, II is true while I and III are false." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402889 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402890 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402891 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402892 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402893 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402893 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402888 1080 #uuid "9247b5bb-55c1-5dcd-9dad-e5cbea588f1a" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402889 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402889 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402889 1084 #uuid "f28e3667-2980-5074-8ca0-7c65c818f580" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402890 1081 "I only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402890 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402890 1084 #uuid "a36c6aa3-5eca-5ce1-a603-385bd52d2612" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402891 1081 "III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402891 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402891 1084 #uuid "cf91ce51-0283-5449-b2fe-9642496d8caa" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402892 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402892 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402892 1084 #uuid "e87dd991-b032-56f7-969b-d3143d2e4eb5" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402893 1081 "II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402893 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402893 1084 #uuid "d16a79db-14b9-542d-af73-6d819fa169a8" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402894 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402895 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402894 1069 "q-47559" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402894 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402894 1071 "![](images/61/613eaf413822013885a22df61a4bf32f7cd763bf11db71ab7b8769e19c0369b0.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=0.$\nII. It is continuous at $x=3.$\nIII. It has removable discontinuities at both $x=0$ and $x=3.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402894 1072 #uuid "66cc33ab-f2ce-599f-8f13-d60a316244d0" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402894 1074 "The function has a discontinuity at $x=0.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(0)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)\\ne f(0)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=0$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nIn the same way, the function has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(3)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=-2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)\\ne f(3)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I and III are true while II is false." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402896 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402897 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402898 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402899 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402900 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402896 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402895 1080 #uuid "8f8a6daf-f494-52bf-bfe7-77e7b41763ac" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402896 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402896 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402896 1084 #uuid "dd4e63c1-9f02-5fd7-949e-98f752ee154d" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402897 1081 "I only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402897 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402897 1084 #uuid "5399ec6b-9f9b-5481-b0b1-7de0826e1d8b" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402898 1081 "III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402898 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402898 1084 #uuid "57b825f2-08f0-5a00-9dfc-852febae5025" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402899 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402899 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402899 1084 #uuid "553afacb-c3c4-5e4f-bddf-bab35e33076b" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402900 1081 "II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402900 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402900 1084 #uuid "6c2d8a1c-1a48-589b-a7fd-3af4c277ad66" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402901 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402902 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402901 1069 "q-4772" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402901 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402901 1071 "The displacement (in centimeters) of an ant moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+3t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds.\nFind the ant's acceleration at $t=10$ seconds." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402901 1072 #uuid "3288674d-b4a5-55ff-8fac-98e0dfe5f073" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402901 1074 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+3t) \\\\  & =2t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+3) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=10,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\na(10)=2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=10$ seconds is $2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402903 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402904 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402905 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402906 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402907 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402905 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402902 1080 #uuid "48976552-dafa-517b-8efc-328d3431eb21" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402903 1081 "8{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402903 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402903 1084 #uuid "dde387b6-d031-5e1d-869d-78a8e279a5e3" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402904 1081 "15{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402904 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402904 1084 #uuid "3c7b5619-6558-57a0-86d6-8a9bcba4ede1" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402905 1081 "2{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402905 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402905 1084 #uuid "9efe4716-2273-55b3-91df-72ec9bf513b2" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402906 1081 "10{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402906 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402906 1084 #uuid "806050ba-b69f-5737-87f4-12b75c80a901" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402907 1081 "4{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402907 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402907 1084 #uuid "a438f893-00a9-5445-880e-2e5cc2012d4b" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402908 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402909 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402908 1069 "q-47918" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402908 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402908 1071 "![](images/4a/4a1843255ea718116bd2daa07f1375a3fb277c47ec8503fec90da824cd714d0b.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. Given that $f(x)$ is defined on the interval $x\\in [-2,10],$ which points represent the global maximum of $f(x)$ ?" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402908 1072 #uuid "126dc5db-7aa0-5e31-885e-35517971a655" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402908 1074 "The global extrema of a function are the lowest or highest points of the function's graph over its entire domain.\n\nThe lowest point is the global minimum, whereas the highest point is the global maximum.\n\nAccording to the graph, the highest point is $D,$ and so this point represents the global maximum of $f(x).$ \n\n**Note:** The point $B$ is not a global maximum, it's a local maximum." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402910 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402911 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402912 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402913 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402914 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402911 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402909 1080 #uuid "e587e32b-f21e-545a-8ef6-e7a910ea785c" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402910 1081 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402910 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402910 1084 #uuid "b6390a69-73ca-5747-ad35-6ad1cc3e50ad" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402911 1081 "$D$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402911 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402911 1084 #uuid "bf810803-9256-56b1-b55f-ffc26fa5e427" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402912 1081 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402912 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402912 1084 #uuid "6f3e8609-ca99-5684-877b-a0d89799e552" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402913 1081 "$C$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402913 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17