 true] [17592186402916 1080 #uuid "01f254e3-3027-52e3-8cb7-edd707cacbbe" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402917 1081 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402917 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402917 1084 #uuid "5af784ce-3cef-5945-8932-b03fe43316e6" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402918 1081 "$B$ and $D$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402918 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402918 1084 #uuid "9673d400-5f29-5ce5-b5e9-8047de8eb008" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402919 1081 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402919 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402919 1084 #uuid "eb5c6830-b8b8-54b9-9b05-279cc0d24408" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402920 1081 "$C$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402920 1084 #uuid "f088b713-a43a-50e7-9574-07ac077ab3d9" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402921 1081 "$B$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402921 1084 #uuid "62bbee0f-e18c-5110-a2d4-144a718f657e" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402923 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402924 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402925 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402926 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402927 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402923 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1080 #uuid "a758672a-df89-5c21-bda2-9147f61578a2" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402923 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402923 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402923 1084 #uuid "d1761688-95e3-5738-a863-ea6cd4b7c723" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402924 1081 "$x=1$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402924 1084 #uuid "9bf0bd1f-bbf9-5956-9fdb-4861ff24950e" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402925 1081 "$x=0$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402925 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402925 1084 #uuid "8361182a-8eda-5e46-8218-dd866302f4a4" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402926 1081 "$x=-3$, $x=0$ and $x=1$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402926 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402926 1084 #uuid "e4f39b69-994d-5142-951e-f121dd4222ef" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402927 1081 "$x=-3$  only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402927 1084 #uuid "d4d4fd26-5931-574f-8d88-1d7ff410bd22" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402929 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1069 "q-48120" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1071 "Given the functions $\\,f(x),\\,g(x)\\,$ and $\\,h(x)\\,$ below, which of them has a point discontinuity at $x=1?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-1 & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ 2(x-1), & x>1\\end{aligned} \\\\  \\\\ g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}3x+2, & x<1 \\\\ 4, & x=1 \\\\ -3x+8, & x>1\\end{aligned} \\\\  \\\\ h(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-1}, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 1, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1072 #uuid "f08cee0d-f749-5e56-a39d-99fa204b19b2" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1074 "Let's check each function, in turn:\n\nLet's check our continuity conditions for $f(x)$ at $x=1:$\n\n- $f(1)=0$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & ={1}^{3}-1=0, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =2(1-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=f(1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nNow, let's check our continuity conditions for $g(x)$ at $x=1:$\n\n- $g(1)=4$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}g(x) & =3(1)+2=5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}g(x) & =-3(1)+8=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=5.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)\\ne g(1)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1.$ It's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=1$ is a point discontinuity. \n\nFinally, let's check our continuity conditions for $h(x)$ at $x=1:$\n\n- $h(1)={e}^{(1-1)}=1$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}h(x) & ={e}^{(1-1)}=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}h(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}h(x)=1.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}h(x)=h(1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nSo, the function $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, only $g(x)$ has a point discontinuity at $x=1.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402930 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402931 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402932 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402933 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402934 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402933 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1080 #uuid "7dd4af99-c768-578a-80d6-2d40aafbe957" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402930 1081 "$f(x)$ and $g(x)$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402930 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402930 1084 #uuid "793b5398-7a91-594d-bf3e-12774bb4d533" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402931 1081 "$f(x)$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402931 1084 #uuid "34d69758-08a3-5130-9d02-5a8a139d1d93" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402932 1081 "$g(x)$ and $h(x)$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402932 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402932 1084 #uuid "1de0e64a-faa1-5969-9784-4c9d1f067325" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402933 1081 "$g(x)$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402933 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402933 1084 #uuid "d85ecdec-99fd-5bc8-94bb-2c2db87123cc" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402934 1081 "$h(x)$ only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402934 1084 #uuid "da0e9431-8013-5bb5-a002-3fc5d3a10ddf" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402936 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1069 "q-48144" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)$ below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3x-1, & x\\ne -1 \\\\ 4, & x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nI. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nII. It has a jump discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nIII. It is continuous at $x=-1.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1072 #uuid "022bd345-534b-5a28-b7c0-bb66d9319957" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1074 "For $x=-1,$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $f(-1)=4$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}(3x-1)=3(-1)-1=-4, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}(3x-1)=3(-1)-1=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-4.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Finally, we check that the value of the limit equals the value of the function: \n\n$$\nf(-1)=4\\ne {lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x).\n$$\n\nSo the value of the limit does not equal the value of the function.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n\nHence, I is true, and II and III are false." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402937 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402938 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402939 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402940 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402941 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402939 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1080 #uuid "3992d45c-afe2-5363-a989-ec3ebd9b8f59" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402937 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402937 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402937 1084 #uuid "a095986c-650b-5ce5-a411-4e76afa98e44" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402938 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402938 1084 #uuid "affc90d5-cd15-5c83-8374-9ef22d10a282" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402939 1081 "I only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402939 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402939 1084 #uuid "7b202b71-8e90-5cb4-a645-b34cefcc87f1" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402940 1081 "III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402940 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402940 1084 #uuid "689bff8b-8178-52e3-be31-da9a10cd172f" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402941 1081 "II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402941 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402941 1084 #uuid "1a544d2b-81d4-5ac0-ab6e-f3ef4a887758" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402943 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1069 "q-48185" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1071 "![](images/78/786d223be90c13335ab80672631dcbef25297688ae9e318928e744ebbf8a5cdf.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. It has a jump discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nII. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nIII. It is continuous at $x=-1.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1072 #uuid "825ab862-b738-5389-82d3-382684f52334" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1074 "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=-1.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(-1)=2$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=-1$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I is true, and II and III are false." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402944 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402945 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402946 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402947 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402948 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402945 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1080 #uuid "39e1e51d-430b-5ea5-a049-7e9e7c4fca2e" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402944 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402944 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402944 1084 #uuid "7fda113a-7bf7-5eb4-99a5-9b1cb83affd3" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402945 1081 "I only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402945 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402945 1084 #uuid "8905c8f3-f5d9-5afc-9051-7fee3195c0bf" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402946 1081 "III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402946 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402946 1084 #uuid "4fc17c2a-cb47-5f11-ada6-66161e86841d" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402947 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402947 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402947 1084 #uuid "580b483e-22b0-57fc-9fde-0dca338c45bf" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402948 1081 "II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402948 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402948 1084 #uuid "a55b19fc-2678-598c-a95e-1ac4b6a20c32" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402949 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402950 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402949 1069 "q-48187" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402949 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402949 1071 "![](images/03/034e2813b404338a1b8d0ecfdb509781f7917e356155474d788d8bd85df0f221.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. It has a point discontinuity at $x=-2.$\nII. It has a jump discontinuity at $x=-2.$\nIII. It is continuous at $x=-2.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402949 1072 #uuid "ed867e40-29b3-530b-96c3-6f5fbbb12043" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402949 1074 "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=-2.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(-2)=2$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)=1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=-2$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, II is true, and I and III are false." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402951 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402952 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402953 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402954 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402955 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402955 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402950 1080 #uuid "73c57e4b-7521-5bbd-a21f-2c62d988da8c" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402951 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402951 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402951 1084 #uuid "a5ab67aa-88f4-5160-8da2-06e0165d98c2" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402952 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402952 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402952 1084 #uuid "94f12f6e-f82b-5487-a2fd-88a2618af1ec" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402953 1081 "I only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402953 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402953 1084 #uuid "a649bf43-5693-588e-b7a4-f5a348f9585a" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402954 1081 "III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402954 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402954 1084 #uuid "d0da8b3f-d34f-50a1-91da-64290158d6db" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402955 1081 "II only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402955 1084 #uuid "7517b44c-4288-5afd-98bb-3306dfffce68" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402957 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1069 "q-48254" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1071 "![](images/a5/a50d4de74cb016b44546791985e5e1fdc519a9b5d2d4943ff24f6d492f4fa031.png)\n\nThe sides of a square decrease in length at a rate of $2\\text{ m/s}.$ At what rate is the area of the square decreasing when the sides are $10\\text{ m}$ long?" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1072 #uuid "60458af0-4d18-5219-97d4-dbd05ed7e66c" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1074 "Let $x$ and $A$ be the length of the sides and the area of the square, respectively. We want to find\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\nThe area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that each side of the square is decreasing at a rate of $2\\,\\text{m/s},$ so we have $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-2.$ Also, when the sides are $10\\,\\text{m},$ we have $x=10.$ Substituting this information into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =(-2)\\cdot 2(10)=-40{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the square decreases at $40\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}/\\text{s}.$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402958 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402959 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402960 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402961 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402962 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402960 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1080 #uuid "03aa2a75-a535-5715-a30a-bcc66a0ca916" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402958 1081 "30{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402958 1084 #uuid "3d26e347-1ad3-5fde-8910-82d6d192a4c0" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402959 1081 "15{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402959 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402959 1084 #uuid "a6bfe9bb-0d95-596e-9565-5b0937d0dee0" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402960 1081 "40{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402960 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402960 1084 #uuid "e338773b-f299-5166-aa17-b7e7ad137b42" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402961 1081 "80{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402961 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402961 1084 #uuid "e07cb7aa-0dfe-5028-8d59-44e5386e6298" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402962 1081 "20{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402962 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402962 1084 #uuid "057ef675-78db-588f-94fd-4a1cdb060767" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402964 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1069 "q-48404" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1071 "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(3,-3)$ and is concave down on the interval $(1,4).$ If ${f}^{′}(3)=4,$ estimate the value of $f(3.2)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=3$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1072 #uuid "23fa4cab-6951-5a21-810d-7733098a8e5c" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(3)+{f}^{′}(3)(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function passes through the point $(3,-3),$ so we have $f(3)=-3.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(3)=4,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-3+4(x-3) \\\\  & =-3+4x-12 \\\\  & =4x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(3.2)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.2) & ≈L(3.2) \\\\  & =4(3.2)-15 \\\\  & =12.8-15 \\\\  & =-2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave down on the interval $(1,4),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is above the graph near $x=3,$ and therefore we have an overestimate." 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402965 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402966 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402967 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402968 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402969 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402965 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1080 #uuid "b7c924a1-67fd-5e0c-8035-7de5293c5ea0" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402965 1081 "$f(3.2)≈-2.2,$ an overestimate" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402965 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402965 1084 #uuid "5cf36fa0-f53d-5a7d-b768-a8a6d96fa3d5" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402966 1081 "$f(3.2)≈-2.6,$ an overestimate" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402966 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402966 1084 #uuid "c863ec26-7875-52c6-8e8e-ef3828506796" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402967 1081 "$f(3.2)≈-2.6,$ an underestimate" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402967 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402967 1084 #uuid "a196f4d2-df4e-518f-b800-04deefc67cdc" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402968 1081 "$f(3.2)≈-2.2,$ an underestimate" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402968 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402968 1084 #uuid "0856fb24-85cf-5798-a1f2-7784442e16d2" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402969 1081 "$f(3.2)≈-3.4,$ an overestimate" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402969 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402969 1084 #uuid "5fdd5bf8-16a7-5589-8bf3-a8302c740846" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402971 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1069 "q-48498" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1071 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,8]?$\n\nI. $g(x)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}$\nII. $s(x)=(x-2)^{2}$\nIII. $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-3}$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1072 #uuid "83188ea1-87cd-5ad1-b8c9-6226665589eb" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1074 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,8],$ the function must be continuous on $[1,8]$ and differentiable on $(1,8).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}$ is continuous on $[1,8]$ and has a cusp only at $x=0,$ which is outside $[1,8],$ hence it is differentiable on $(1,8).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $s(x)=(x-2)^{2}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[1,8]$ and differentiable on $(1,8).$ Therefore, $s(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-3}$ is not defined at $x=3$, so it is not continuous at $x=3$, which means it is not continuous on $[1,8].$ Therefore, $h(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and II satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,8].$" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402972 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402973 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402974 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402975 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402976 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1077 "selection" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402975 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1080 #uuid "53957ce4-c21c-52c2-8684-73966d29c5a3" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402972 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533490 17592186045585 true] [17592186402972 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 1319